  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "c4f5ebd0-1155-4185-bd47-3ebe45dd4653",
      "name": "📌 Overview – How This Workflow Works",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1424,
        -560
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 796,
        "height": 684,
        "content": "## 📧 Missed Sale Automation – EDI Order Gap Detection\n\n### How it works\nWhen a sales report arrives by email (typically an EDI export from your ERP or warehouse system as a CSV attachment), this workflow picks it up automatically. It extracts the CSV, then loops through each line item one at a time. For each row, it builds a unique key from the customer name, PO number, and SAP material code, and checks whether a Missed Sales record already exists in GoHighLevel custom objects. New records are created with all relevant fields — PO number, SAP code, missed quantity, unit price, missed value, and rejection reason. After creation, the record is linked to the matching GHL opportunity (found by PO number lookup). Existing records are skipped. This gives your sales team a live list of missed sales opportunities they can act on directly inside GHL.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. Set up **Gmail OAuth2** on the Gmail Trigger and Get Gmail Message Content nodes — configure the trigger to watch for emails containing your EDI report attachment.\n2. Add your **GHL (LeadConnector) Private Integration Token** as `YOUR_GHL_API_TOKEN` in the Authorization header of all five HTTP Request nodes.\n3. Replace `YOUR_GHL_LOCATION_ID` with your GHL sub-account location ID in all HTTP nodes.\n4. Replace `YOUR_GHL_ASSOCIATION_ID` with the association ID that links Missed Sales records to Opportunities in your GHL account.\n5. Activate the Gmail trigger."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "7db62f54-2911-4a48-b68e-ed24edb1c05b",
      "name": "Section – Email Trigger & CSV Extraction",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -528,
        160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 968,
        "height": 456,
        "content": "## 📨 Email Trigger & CSV Extraction\nWatches for incoming emails matching your filter, fetches the full message, and extracts the CSV from the attachment. Each row in the CSV becomes one item in the loop — one missed sale line from the EDI report."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b5d1f864-c635-49b3-880c-e67f27d9056a",
      "name": "Section – Field Mapping & Dedup Check",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        304,
        -352
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 860,
        "height": 456,
        "content": "## 🔑 Field Mapping & Deduplication Check\nBuilds a composite unique key from customer name + PO number + SAP material code, maps all CSV fields to clean variable names, then checks the prefetched missed sales records to see if this row was already processed — skipping duplicates without making extra API calls."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "857659c8-4ce4-45c4-9884-ecc0782eab35",
      "name": "Section – GHL Record Creation & Linking",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1216,
        -144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1100,
        "height": 712,
        "content": "## 🏗️ GHL Record Creation & Opportunity Linking\nFor new missed sales: creates a custom object record in GHL with all EDI fields, then finds the matching GHL opportunity by PO number and creates an association between the new record and the opportunity. If no matching opportunity exists, the record is still created unlinked."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
